<template>
  <screen class="app">
    <text class="title">computed and effect, inside a component</text>
    <text class="lead">Each row derives its own line total and writes its own note. Both live in the component's script and run once per instance, in that instance's scope: the steppers move one row's numbers and leave the others alone. The sale switch is a document signal, and every row's effect is subscribed to it because every row read it.</text>

    <view class="rows">
      <cart-row :label="&quot;flat white&quot;" :price="4" />
      <cart-row :label="&quot;sourdough&quot;" :price="6" />
      <cart-row :label="&quot;olive oil&quot;" :price="11" />
    </view>

    <view class="btn" @tap="sale = !sale">
      <text class="btn-label">toggle the sale</text>
    </view>
  </screen>
</template>

<style>
  .app {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 28px;
    background: #1e1e2e;
  }

  .title { color: #cdd6f4; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; }
  .lead { color: #9399b2; font-size: 13px; max-width: 620px; }
  .rows { display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start; }

  .btn {
    padding: 8px 14px;
    background: #89b4fa;
    border-radius: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
    max-width: 160px;
  }

  .btn:hover { background: #b4befe; }
  .btn-label { color: #11111b; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; }
</style>

<script>
  use components::cart_row;

  let currency = signal("$");
  let sale = signal(false);
</script>
